cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "TENET: A Verification-First TypeScript Agent Framework with BENCHMARKS Gated in CI"
message: "If you use TENET in academic work, please cite this software."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "TENET contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/zakky8/TENET"
url: "https://github.com/zakky8/TENET"
abstract: >
  TENET is an open-source TypeScript agent framework with a multi-judge
  atomic-claim hallucination verifier (Vectara HHEM-2.1 adapter),
  pre-tool-call governance with approval gates and structured audit
  trail, WASM-sandboxed tool execution with capability tokens
  (wasmtime adapter), Model Context Protocol (MCP) OAuth gateway with
  RFC 9207 issuer validation, ten channel surfaces (Discord, Slack,
  Telegram, MS Teams, web widget, REST, gRPC, and four ticketing
  webhooks: Zendesk, Intercom, Freshdesk, ServiceNow), and a
  measurement plane (hermetic stub SUT plus a real-ChatModel harness
  against a public-shape dataset slice) whose BENCHMARKS dimensions
  are gated in continuous integration on every pull request. The
  framework is designed to be hardened by construction (zero
  high-severity CVEs across the 2025-2026 disclosure window) and
  source-grounded by default. Apache-2.0 licensed.
keywords:
  - AI agent framework
  - TypeScript
  - hallucination detection
  - multi-judge verifier
  - HHEM-2.1
  - Vectara
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - RAG
  - WASM sandbox
  - capability tokens
  - Model Context Protocol
  - MCP
  - OAuth
  - governance
  - approval gates
  - audit trail
  - OpenTelemetry GenAI
  - source grounding
  - prompt injection
  - LangChain alternative
  - LangGraph alternative
  - agent benchmarks
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.0.0
date-released: 2026-06-04
